{"id": "EUVD-2026-86089", "enisaUuid": "3e49869d-a9dc-3502-b3a6-e3e215dc4089", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/rds: Don't sleep inside rds_ib_conn_path_shutdown\n\nNew rds rdma self tests exposed a hang when tearing down\nthe ib network configs.  This is caused by the shutdown worker\nthread sleeping on the wait_event call, which blocks other work\nitems in the queue. Fix this by changing wait_event to\nwait_event timeout, and looping until the wait check succeeds.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:04:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:58:56", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b3621acf640e32dcb986d9b3767f2387f29dad05", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac0bc28da5150c4fa81a76172fff5ec70f2063eb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/934a6381c79d815680c955d676791322e020bfda", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/07a348d48e589b91a0d5a5cfa0de137cc703fabf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/db22e77df66353f1299153f6fa9620a2825bc63f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/caa51e6da596ed6008cd06605a725568b8e7be4e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/16f48efaeb6991193fb7775c577f06f5b20b0c90"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rj2j-ff3c-jjm2", "CVE-2026-97491"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ca041d6-f746-381e-99a0-58a801eb7b32", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ec16227e14141e4fd7ae76354c09dadfe2449d9e <934a6381c79d815680c955d676791322e020bfda"}, {"id": "31dbc288-ff08-3f32-bc66-8103937b3e1e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "49485074-385b-3660-a2f1-723074ed93a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.30"}, {"id": "60693c14-9356-30e6-8492-c513f9c6510c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "65abf747-1b74-3271-ad10-cbe9506d72e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor"